1
00:01:30,490 --> 00:01:34,970
[AWAKEN]

2
00:01:35,690 --> 00:01:37,830
[Episode 3]

3
00:01:38,479 --> 00:01:39,340
Eight bamboos.

4
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:43,310
I win!

5
00:02:15,190 --> 00:02:16,470
Who wants to kill me?

6
00:02:18,910 --> 00:02:20,960
T-The Chongqing Hurricane Team.

7
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,470
Why didn't Captain Tao come himself?

8
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:33,570
Does he not take me seriously,

9
00:02:36,520 --> 00:02:37,800
or are you lying?

10
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:02,280
I... I really

11
00:03:02,280 --> 00:03:04,590
work for the Chongqing Hurricane Team!

12
00:03:04,590 --> 00:03:06,710
But the one who wants to kill you
is Yu Yingxiang.

13
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:08,280
He gave me 2,000 yuan.

14
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:10,240
Yu Yingxiang?

15
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,960
Yes.

16
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:13,140
Li Moqun's lackey?

17
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,730
Yes, yes.

18
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:20,290
Is No. 76 really working with
the Hurricane Team?

19
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:22,000
Yes.

20
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:25,520
Yes.

21
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:27,960
Was it you who killed Suzuki?

22
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:29,710
No.

23
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,190
Nanjing has already sent people
to investigate,

24
00:03:32,190 --> 00:03:33,790
and you're still lying to me?

25
00:03:33,870 --> 00:03:36,000
Didn't we agree on

26
00:03:36,079 --> 00:03:37,280
no killing back then?

27
00:03:38,710 --> 00:03:41,240
It was an accidental killing
by the Japanese.

28
00:03:41,310 --> 00:03:42,770
Are you telling the truth?

29
00:03:44,579 --> 00:03:46,570
I still want to keep working with you.

30
00:03:46,570 --> 00:03:48,170
I have no reason to lie to you.

31
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:52,590
Those Japanese bastards.

32
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,870
They caused the trouble themselves,

33
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:55,870
and now they want me to take the fall.

34
00:03:58,920 --> 00:04:02,190
I'm looking for someone
who was involved in Project Slumber.

35
00:04:02,190 --> 00:04:03,280
Help me ask around.

36
00:04:11,190 --> 00:04:12,870
Nanjing sent an inspector

37
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:14,750
to investigate corruption.

38
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,680
It's a bit awkward for me right now.

39
00:04:17,829 --> 00:04:19,890
Finding a scapegoat to close the case

40
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:22,690
shouldn't be too hard for you, right?

41
00:04:24,920 --> 00:04:26,450
I'll figure something out.

42
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:41,570
I came today to let you know, General,

43
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:44,640
that I already have a lead on the person

44
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:46,760
who betrayed Mr. Suzuki's whereabouts.

45
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:51,530
[Major-General Kagesa, Chief of
the Japanese Plum Blossom Agency]

46
00:04:48,950 --> 00:04:52,120
Even Director Li's investigation
turned up nothing,

47
00:04:52,950 --> 00:04:54,830
yet Inspector Su, you've only just
arrived in Shanghai,

48
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:56,430
and you already found a lead?

49
00:04:59,070 --> 00:05:01,040
Perhaps Director Li
has simply been too busy

50
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,700
to give it his full attention.

51
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,040
Too busy?

52
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:07,690
From what I understand,

53
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,070
several recent extortion cases

54
00:05:09,070 --> 00:05:10,680
involving Shanghai's business community

55
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,430
have all been linked to No. 76.

56
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,600
I'm afraid Director Li
has been focusing his energy

57
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:16,430
on lining his own pockets

58
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:20,070
rather than cracking down on the NBIS
and the Communists.

59
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:30,270
It seems, Inspector Su, that you came to
Shanghai at exactly the right time.

60
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:32,630
We need someone

61
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:34,430
as conscientious as you.

62
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:39,430
Before I came, Chairman Wang specifically
instructed me

63
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:41,600
not to let you down, General Kagesa.

64
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:48,510
Then we'll be counting on you,
Inspector Su.

65
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,800
Please feel free to act with confidence.

66
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:54,800
I'll give you my full support.

67
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,950
Much obliged.

68
00:05:58,560 --> 00:05:59,600
It's my duty.

69
00:06:00,640 --> 00:06:01,440
Captain Cang.

70
00:06:09,630 --> 00:06:10,430
Inspector Su.

71
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:12,750
Where's Director Li?

72
00:06:13,310 --> 00:06:14,110
In his office.

73
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,660
You guys go find Yu Yingxiang.

74
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:29,000
Freshly brewed. Try it.

75
00:06:29,430 --> 00:06:31,120
I've found the assassin

76
00:06:31,360 --> 00:06:33,220
who got away at the train station.

77
00:06:34,750 --> 00:06:36,280
Yu Yingxiang works for you.

78
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:38,140
He sent someone to kill me—

79
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:39,840
did you know about this?

80
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:45,530
Yu Yingxiang has the nerve
to do something like that?

81
00:06:47,750 --> 00:06:48,430
Guards!

82
00:06:50,310 --> 00:06:51,750
Bring Yu Yingxiang here at once.

83
00:06:51,750 --> 00:06:52,310
Yes, sir.

84
00:07:02,870 --> 00:07:03,560
Excuse me.

85
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,170
Chief Yu didn't come to work today.

86
00:07:08,190 --> 00:07:09,870
Please, everyone, go have some tea first.

87
00:07:09,870 --> 00:07:11,670
I'll try to get in touch with him.

88
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:14,690
Seal the place off.

89
00:07:15,830 --> 00:07:16,560
Seal it off?

90
00:07:22,030 --> 00:07:25,690
I'm afraid, Director Li, you don't know
where he is either, do you?

91
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:32,250
We are currently looking for him.

92
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:34,040
It's not about looking for him—

93
00:07:34,159 --> 00:07:35,620
it's about arresting him.

94
00:07:42,610 --> 00:07:45,360
An arrest requires a warrant, doesn't it?

95
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:50,310
Captain Cang has failed
to do his job properly.

96
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:51,310
Arrest him first!

97
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:59,470
Ouch, ouch, ouch!

98
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:02,780
Follow Inspector Su's orders

99
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,400
and arrest Yu Yingxiang.

100
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:05,530
Inspector.

101
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,600
Do you think Li Moqun

102
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,460
will hand Yu Yingxiang over to us?

103
00:08:08,950 --> 00:08:10,360
Keep an eye on Cang Guanglian.

104
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,290
Follow them and find Yu Yingxiang.

105
00:08:12,430 --> 00:08:13,160
Understood.

106
00:08:18,830 --> 00:08:19,960
Where's the ledger?

107
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:20,950
It's with me.

108
00:08:21,240 --> 00:08:23,040
I'll send someone to collect it,

109
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,360
and then have you escorted
out of Shanghai.

110
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:26,000
Okay.

111
00:08:35,870 --> 00:08:41,720
♪ Clear waters stir in the cool breeze ♪

112
00:08:44,510 --> 00:08:49,720
♪ Waters stir in the cool breeze ♪

113
00:08:51,790 --> 00:08:55,360
♪ Summer lingers long ♪

114
00:09:30,550 --> 00:09:32,030
What kind of day is this?

115
00:09:33,480 --> 00:09:36,080
Even drinking water's enough
to make me choke.

116
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,200
Let's go.

117
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,490
I'm here to collect photos.

118
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,500
Do you remember me?

119
00:10:25,150 --> 00:10:27,280
Your camera's American-made, right?

120
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:29,260
Chen Kailai, he's asking you.

121
00:10:30,310 --> 00:10:31,070
It's German.

122
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:37,070
I heard they have color film now.

123
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:39,420
Yes, but I still prefer black-and-white.

124
00:10:39,550 --> 00:10:40,550
Black is black,

125
00:10:40,550 --> 00:10:41,610
and white is white.

126
00:10:43,630 --> 00:10:44,490
Master, don't!

127
00:10:52,230 --> 00:10:52,920
Master!

128
00:10:56,790 --> 00:10:59,120
Chen Kailai, you're also a Communist!

129
00:11:12,960 --> 00:11:14,820
I still prefer black-and-white.

130
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:17,670
Black is black,

131
00:11:18,080 --> 00:11:19,150
and white is white.

132
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:22,180
I still prefer black-and-white.

133
00:11:22,270 --> 00:11:23,320
Black is black,

134
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,500
and white is white.

135
00:11:27,510 --> 00:11:30,030
I heard they have color film now.

136
00:11:30,330 --> 00:11:31,210
They do,

137
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,870
but mine is black-and-white.

138
00:11:39,910 --> 00:11:41,390
Do we know each other?

139
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,390
It was Miss Shen.

140
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,200
♪ Matchmaker ♪

141
00:11:56,150 --> 00:12:00,270
♪ Sitting alone in your chamber ♪

142
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:09,840
♪ Brooding over your loneliness ♪

143
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:25,320
♪ Why not go to the garden
to lift your spirits? ♪

144
00:12:40,600 --> 00:12:42,360
Life is unpredictable.

145
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:26,630
It's truly a small world.

146
00:13:50,400 --> 00:13:51,390
What's this piece of junk?

147
00:13:51,390 --> 00:13:53,590
Gentlemen, are you here for a bath or...

148
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:57,760
Sorry.

149
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:58,360
Are you okay?

150
00:13:58,360 --> 00:13:59,150
I'm fine.

151
00:13:59,320 --> 00:14:00,320
I'm okay.

152
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:09,670
You...

153
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:32,960
I didn't expect it to be you!

154
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,500
Du Huangqiao.

155
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:52,980
Get the hell up!

156
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:54,510
Cover my retreat,

157
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:56,650
or I'll have you court-martialed!

158
00:14:59,750 --> 00:15:01,810
You really do look like a darn beggar.

159
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:09,270
Weren't you going to have me
court-martialed?

160
00:15:09,510 --> 00:15:10,310
Come on, then.

161
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:13,840
Battalion Commander Du.

162
00:15:14,360 --> 00:15:15,160
Come on, then!

163
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:20,550
Run!

164
00:15:54,510 --> 00:15:56,150
You broke this watch.

165
00:15:56,320 --> 00:15:58,150
I'll give you 10 minutes to fix it.

166
00:15:58,150 --> 00:15:59,350
If you can't fix it,

167
00:16:00,030 --> 00:16:01,160
I'll fix your wagon.

168
00:16:31,130 --> 00:16:32,840
A water-damaged watch is not hard to fix.

169
00:16:32,840 --> 00:16:34,300
Just drying it out will do.

170
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,530
The real challenge is
putting it back together.

171
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:41,200
But how's a blind man like me
supposed to do that?

172
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:42,030
Could it be

173
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:45,330
that God wants to take my life?

174
00:16:54,200 --> 00:16:56,150
What's going on? What's with
all this commotion today?

175
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:57,320
With all these trucks and cars.

176
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,440
Excuse me. Make way.

177
00:16:58,440 --> 00:16:59,870
And so many people gathered around.

178
00:16:59,870 --> 00:17:00,420
Don't look.

179
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:01,390
Why are you sticking your nose into
other people's business?

180
00:17:01,390 --> 00:17:02,630
It's not other people's business.

181
00:17:02,630 --> 00:17:04,310
That guy's clearly giving him a hard time.

182
00:17:04,310 --> 00:17:05,680
Do you want to lose your life
or something?

183
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:07,069
All the more reason to step in

184
00:17:07,069 --> 00:17:08,960
if he's being deliberately mistreated.

185
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:09,349
What's your business here?

186
00:17:09,349 --> 00:17:10,750
To fix your boss's watch.

187
00:17:15,109 --> 00:17:16,310
Since you're blind,

188
00:17:17,109 --> 00:17:18,349
I'll be your eyes.

189
00:17:19,069 --> 00:17:20,240
This won't end well.

190
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:22,240
This hothead

191
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:23,829
is impossible to rein in.

192
00:17:23,829 --> 00:17:25,400
He's going to get himself into
serious trouble sooner or later.

193
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:26,400
Give me the watch.

194
00:17:28,030 --> 00:17:28,760
You teach me.

195
00:17:30,030 --> 00:17:31,440
I know a thing or two.

196
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:33,400
He said 10 minutes.

197
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,350
I'll time it for you. No need to panic.

198
00:17:35,350 --> 00:17:35,960
Right.

199
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:37,560
Right, we'll time it for him.

200
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,000
First, open the front cover—

201
00:17:47,680 --> 00:17:49,590
the side with the glass.

202
00:17:56,510 --> 00:17:57,270
Mr. Zhao.

203
00:17:59,510 --> 00:18:00,710
What brings you here?

204
00:18:01,440 --> 00:18:03,110
Take out the balance wheel.

205
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,930
Inside, there's an upper cover
and a lower cover.

206
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:12,240
Carefully remove them.

207
00:18:28,350 --> 00:18:30,400
Now, install the connecting shaft.

208
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:45,970
Lighter.

209
00:18:50,310 --> 00:18:51,480
A-Adjutant Cui?

210
00:18:52,550 --> 00:18:53,680
You got here so fast.

211
00:19:00,030 --> 00:19:01,690
He just died a short while ago.

212
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,280
That's right.

213
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:07,270
I swear to God,

214
00:19:07,270 --> 00:19:09,400
he was already like this when I came in.

215
00:19:09,550 --> 00:19:10,240
L-Look.

216
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:12,250
He was strangled to death.

217
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:14,510
Good thing you showed up.

218
00:19:14,510 --> 00:19:17,040
Otherwise, I'd never be able to
clear my name.

219
00:19:19,750 --> 00:19:21,750
Inspector Su needs an explanation.

220
00:19:23,050 --> 00:19:24,180
Sure. Investigate.

221
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,900
Investigate thoroughly.

222
00:19:27,830 --> 00:19:28,440
Done.

223
00:19:31,240 --> 00:19:32,370
Exactly 10 minutes.

224
00:19:47,240 --> 00:19:48,370
Laugh one more time.

225
00:19:49,070 --> 00:19:50,330
Go ahead, laugh again,

226
00:19:50,550 --> 00:19:52,070
and I'll put a bullet
through your windpipe,

227
00:19:52,070 --> 00:19:54,600
so you'll laugh with a loud whoosh
from now on.

228
00:19:56,400 --> 00:19:57,110
Officer,

229
00:19:58,400 --> 00:20:00,240
you're going to kill someone
in broad daylight?

230
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,640
This is a bathhouse, not a slaughterhouse.

231
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:07,330
You've got some nerve.

232
00:20:09,400 --> 00:20:10,200
Let me tell you something:

233
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:12,480
I never kill people without reason.

234
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,500
It's just that my gun has a nasty habit

235
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,000
of going off on its own.

236
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:22,400
Want to see it happen again?

237
00:20:27,790 --> 00:20:31,050
Someone was just killed
in the special care room next door.

238
00:20:34,070 --> 00:20:35,310
Do any of you know

239
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:37,710
who the killer is?

240
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,160
Do you know?

241
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,400
Was it you who killed him?

242
00:21:07,490 --> 00:21:08,210
No.

243
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:10,130
I-I'm blind.

244
00:21:10,550 --> 00:21:12,240
How could I possibly kill someone?

245
00:21:12,240 --> 00:21:14,640
Haven't you killed enough people already?

246
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,480
I...

247
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,240
I'm blind now,

248
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:19,330
and my leg's crippled.

249
00:21:19,550 --> 00:21:21,210
I can't possibly kill anyone.

250
00:21:22,110 --> 00:21:23,310
Crippled?

251
00:21:27,080 --> 00:21:29,560
Your leg's crippled?

252
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,640
Serves you right!

253
00:21:45,750 --> 00:21:47,070
Back during the battle in Nanjing,

254
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:48,730
why did you run off on your own?

255
00:21:54,480 --> 00:21:55,350
And blind, huh?

256
00:21:57,340 --> 00:21:58,690
A blind man can read fortunes—

257
00:21:58,690 --> 00:22:00,150
and he can take lives, too.

258
00:22:00,790 --> 00:22:02,110
You strangled that man

259
00:22:02,110 --> 00:22:03,880
with a rope just now, didn't you?

260
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:04,510
No.

261
00:22:04,510 --> 00:22:06,200
I... Even if I...

262
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:09,830
I can spare your life

263
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:12,640
and just put a bullet
through your stomach.

264
00:22:15,160 --> 00:22:16,270
Even if

265
00:22:17,160 --> 00:22:18,120
I wanted to,

266
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,080
I wouldn't have the guts.

267
00:22:21,720 --> 00:22:24,070
I knew you didn't have the guts.

268
00:22:25,510 --> 00:22:28,790
That battle in Nanjing scared the fight
right out of you, didn't it?

269
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:29,550
Tell me,

270
00:22:30,880 --> 00:22:33,400
how do you expect
to stand up to the Japanese?

271
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,160
You coward.

272
00:22:41,030 --> 00:22:43,290
Who was in the special care room just now?

273
00:22:51,350 --> 00:22:52,110
Tell me.

274
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:53,920
It... It wasn't me.

275
00:23:01,550 --> 00:23:02,350
You say it.

276
00:23:10,550 --> 00:23:11,960
You...

277
00:23:19,590 --> 00:23:20,450
You fixed this?

278
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
How did you fix it?

279
00:23:26,790 --> 00:23:29,120
With the head you're pointing your gun at.

280
00:23:35,790 --> 00:23:37,680
Being able to fix a watch
under those circumstances—

281
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:39,080
you're very meticulous.

282
00:23:39,770 --> 00:23:41,700
You've got the makings of a killer.

283
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:42,880
I'd bet it was him.

284
00:23:44,310 --> 00:23:46,030
Since Inspector Su wants an explanation,

285
00:23:46,030 --> 00:23:47,560
there's your explanation.

286
00:23:48,200 --> 00:23:48,930
It wasn't me.

287
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,910
Were you in the special care room
just now?

288
00:23:56,910 --> 00:23:57,500
I was,

289
00:23:58,280 --> 00:23:59,620
but I don't know what happened.

290
00:23:59,620 --> 00:24:00,780
There's no way I did it.

291
00:24:00,780 --> 00:24:02,370
Cut the crap. Take him away.

292
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:03,160
Yes, sir.

293
00:24:05,310 --> 00:24:06,370
What are you doing?

294
00:24:06,590 --> 00:24:07,240
Why are you arresting me?

295
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:07,790
Move.

296
00:24:08,120 --> 00:24:09,070
Officer,

297
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:11,570
what gives you the right
to just take him away like that?

298
00:24:11,570 --> 00:24:13,410
You've really got some nerve.

299
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:15,920
Even if I wanted to
take everyone in Shanghai away,

300
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:17,480
all it would take is one word from me.

301
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,610
Now get out of my way!

302
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:19,720
-Take him away!
-Move!

303
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:20,480
Let me go!

304
00:24:21,480 --> 00:24:22,070
Move!

305
00:24:22,070 --> 00:24:23,110
It wasn't me!

306
00:24:23,110 --> 00:24:23,720
Kailai!

307
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:25,680
-I'm just a photographer!
-Kailai!

308
00:24:25,680 --> 00:24:26,480
It wasn't me!

309
00:24:27,270 --> 00:24:28,070
Let go!

310
00:24:59,960 --> 00:25:00,720
Du,

311
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:03,480
you're lucky today.

312
00:25:03,560 --> 00:25:05,360
I'll spare your worthless life.

313
00:25:05,750 --> 00:25:07,200
But if I ever get upset,

314
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:08,300
this gun of mine

315
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:10,160
is sure to go off.

316
00:25:39,830 --> 00:25:40,760
Leifeng Pagoda.

317
00:25:41,830 --> 00:25:43,630
How long have you been in hiding?

318
00:25:44,780 --> 00:25:46,380
Exactly 2 years and 3 months.

319
00:25:47,390 --> 00:25:48,590
Stay in hiding.

320
00:25:57,070 --> 00:25:58,070
Mr. Zhao?

321
00:25:59,640 --> 00:26:00,440
Mr. Zhao?

322
00:26:03,960 --> 00:26:05,550
Soaking too long in water that hot

323
00:26:05,550 --> 00:26:06,640
could be fatal.

324
00:26:06,960 --> 00:26:09,960
I've prepared some top-quality
Longjing tea for you.

325
00:26:27,170 --> 00:26:28,890
You say you didn't kill him.

326
00:26:30,440 --> 00:26:31,590
Then tell me,

327
00:26:32,430 --> 00:26:35,090
what exactly happened
in the special care room?

328
00:26:40,920 --> 00:26:42,110
That's all

329
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:43,480
I saw.

330
00:26:48,270 --> 00:26:49,440
So you're saying

331
00:26:50,960 --> 00:26:53,160
someone sneaked into the special care room

332
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:54,560
and killed Yu Yingxiang.

333
00:26:54,880 --> 00:26:55,920
Whoever did it

334
00:26:56,580 --> 00:26:59,140
knew the bathhouse inside and out

335
00:26:59,270 --> 00:27:01,800
and could move around
without being noticed.

336
00:27:04,030 --> 00:27:05,400
If it wasn't you,

337
00:27:06,070 --> 00:27:07,870
then who else could it have been?

338
00:27:15,110 --> 00:27:17,110
Mr. Zhao, have some fruit.

339
00:27:17,240 --> 00:27:17,920
Thank you.

340
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:19,720
With something this big happening,

341
00:27:19,720 --> 00:27:21,920
I thought you'd have gone home already.

342
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:25,240
Nothing matters more than
enjoying yourself.

343
00:27:25,830 --> 00:27:26,480
Why?

344
00:27:27,400 --> 00:27:30,400
Because we're all going to die eventually,
aren't we?

345
00:27:30,680 --> 00:27:33,790
Mr. Zhao, my friend was arrested
by No. 76.

346
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,310
You are...

347
00:27:36,920 --> 00:27:38,270
We met at the station.

348
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:40,440
And the photographer, Chen Kailai.

349
00:27:40,920 --> 00:27:42,880
Yeah, they're both my family.

350
00:27:43,350 --> 00:27:45,010
The photo studio just opened,

351
00:27:45,110 --> 00:27:47,920
and now it's gotten caught up in
something like this.

352
00:27:47,920 --> 00:27:49,790
Chen Kailai is as law-abiding
as they come.

353
00:27:49,790 --> 00:27:51,310
He wouldn't even have the nerve
to kill a chicken,

354
00:27:51,310 --> 00:27:52,480
let alone a person.

355
00:27:53,110 --> 00:27:55,170
There must be
some kind of misunderstanding here.

356
00:27:55,170 --> 00:27:55,960
Mr. Zhao,

357
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,030
do you think

358
00:27:57,350 --> 00:27:58,680
you could figure something out

359
00:27:58,680 --> 00:27:59,350
and help us?

360
00:28:00,920 --> 00:28:02,270
What can I do?

361
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,240
I warned him long ago

362
00:28:05,830 --> 00:28:08,000
that Shanghai isn't an easy place
to get by,

363
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,530
and I told him to be careful.

364
00:28:12,480 --> 00:28:13,440
Mr. Zhao,

365
00:28:15,240 --> 00:28:16,200
name your price.

366
00:28:18,970 --> 00:28:20,780
I don't know if money will help,

367
00:28:21,310 --> 00:28:23,170
but coming to me certainly won't.

368
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:25,840
Don't waste your money on me.

369
00:28:27,160 --> 00:28:28,960
Try pulling some other strings.

370
00:29:37,640 --> 00:29:38,750
You want me

371
00:29:39,560 --> 00:29:40,730
to finger Battalion Commander Du?

372
00:29:40,730 --> 00:29:42,660
What Battalion Commander D-D-Du?

373
00:29:43,100 --> 00:29:44,230
That blind bastard.

374
00:29:46,790 --> 00:29:47,920
You're right, sir.

375
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:50,010
How could a blind man

376
00:29:51,070 --> 00:29:52,400
possibly kill someone?

377
00:29:53,880 --> 00:29:55,140
You've got some nerve.

378
00:29:56,550 --> 00:29:57,950
You're right, actually.

379
00:29:58,240 --> 00:29:59,170
If it wasn't him,

380
00:29:59,720 --> 00:30:01,180
then it must have been you.

381
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:02,240
It wasn't me.

382
00:30:03,720 --> 00:30:04,450
It wasn't me.

383
00:30:04,550 --> 00:30:05,070
Come on.

384
00:30:06,830 --> 00:30:07,560
Look at this.

385
00:30:09,510 --> 00:30:10,570
Just a little twist

386
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:11,930
and a little pry,

387
00:30:12,420 --> 00:30:14,750
and the whole fingernail comes right off.

388
00:30:14,900 --> 00:30:17,480
They say your fingers
are connected to your heart.

389
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:18,810
Do you think it'll hurt?

390
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:19,470
Yes.

391
00:30:20,270 --> 00:30:22,000
It hurts just hearing about it.

392
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:23,550
So whose life is more important:

393
00:30:23,550 --> 00:30:25,280
that blind bastard's or yours?

394
00:30:25,350 --> 00:30:26,000
Mine.

395
00:30:26,070 --> 00:30:26,880
That's right.

396
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:28,660
Now tell me—

397
00:30:29,550 --> 00:30:30,610
who was the killer?

398
00:30:32,510 --> 00:30:33,640
It really wasn't me.

399
00:30:33,750 --> 00:30:34,640
Then who was it?

400
00:30:35,030 --> 00:30:35,890
I didn't see it.

401
00:30:40,110 --> 00:30:42,000
Are you really that desperate to die?

402
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:43,400
All for some scumbag?

403
00:30:50,880 --> 00:30:51,830
Du the Blind

404
00:30:53,110 --> 00:30:54,240
is really a good guy.

405
00:30:55,240 --> 00:30:56,770
You don't know a damn thing!

406
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,240
A good guy?

407
00:30:59,920 --> 00:31:01,480
He should have died in Nanjing.

408
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:03,010
He doesn't deserve to live!

409
00:31:04,790 --> 00:31:05,590
Get the hell up

410
00:31:05,880 --> 00:31:07,140
and hold the position!

411
00:31:07,350 --> 00:31:08,110
Or

412
00:31:08,200 --> 00:31:09,270
I'll have you court-martialed!

413
00:31:09,270 --> 00:31:10,070
Commander.

414
00:31:10,110 --> 00:31:11,370
We're so outnumbered.

415
00:31:11,480 --> 00:31:13,680
Are you sending our men to their deaths?

416
00:31:14,310 --> 00:31:16,440
I'll go find Commander Tang
for reinforcements.

417
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:17,710
You hold the position here!

418
00:31:17,710 --> 00:31:19,160
Commander, but...

419
00:31:19,350 --> 00:31:20,350
Trust me!

420
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:24,240
Guys, cover the Battalion Commander!

421
00:31:35,960 --> 00:31:37,070
Japs!

422
00:31:37,310 --> 00:31:38,000
Bring it on!

423
00:31:40,510 --> 00:31:42,720
He sold us all out.

424
00:31:42,720 --> 00:31:44,640
Do you still think he's a good guy?

425
00:31:47,720 --> 00:31:49,580
The Battalion Commander Du I know

426
00:31:50,330 --> 00:31:51,330
isn't like that.

427
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:03,200
Go on.

428
00:32:04,270 --> 00:32:05,200
Get out of here

429
00:32:05,350 --> 00:32:06,240
and leave Nanjing.

430
00:32:06,240 --> 00:32:08,000
Three or four kilometers east
is the refugee camp.

431
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:08,480
Go on!

432
00:32:08,480 --> 00:32:09,480
-Hurry up, hurry up.
-Move.

433
00:32:09,480 --> 00:32:10,160
Hurry up!

434
00:32:13,070 --> 00:32:14,200
Where are you going?

435
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:15,160
I'm going back.

436
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:16,270
We can't abandon our positions.

437
00:32:16,270 --> 00:32:17,310
Everyone knows

438
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:18,900
Nanjing can't be held any longer.

439
00:32:18,900 --> 00:32:21,400
Even if we can't hold it,
we still have to defend it!

440
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:23,110
If Nanjing falls, what's next?

441
00:32:23,110 --> 00:32:24,830
We'll have to fight for Hankou.
If Hankou falls,

442
00:32:24,830 --> 00:32:25,610
we'll have to fight for Chongqing.

443
00:32:25,610 --> 00:32:27,750
And if we don't hold Chongqing,
we'll have to keep retreating!

444
00:32:27,750 --> 00:32:29,030
If this continues, the entire country

445
00:32:29,030 --> 00:32:30,350
will fall into the hands of the Japanese!

446
00:32:30,350 --> 00:32:31,950
Where else can we retreat to?

447
00:32:58,790 --> 00:33:00,070
Rubbish!

448
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:02,710
Still talking back, huh?

449
00:33:03,200 --> 00:33:04,110
Still trying to play tough, huh?

450
00:33:04,110 --> 00:33:04,720
Boss.

451
00:33:05,970 --> 00:33:08,170
Director Li is back and wants to see you.

452
00:33:13,360 --> 00:33:15,710
Qing, rip out all his fingernails.

453
00:33:15,920 --> 00:33:16,510
Yes, sir.

454
00:33:30,110 --> 00:33:31,350
If it weren't for saving you,

455
00:33:31,350 --> 00:33:32,620
he wouldn't have been taken away.

456
00:33:32,620 --> 00:33:33,590
And here you are, still playing

457
00:33:33,590 --> 00:33:36,320
that lousy three-stringed instrument
of yours.

458
00:33:38,270 --> 00:33:39,930
He still owes us a lot of money.

459
00:33:40,360 --> 00:33:41,830
Stop thinking about money.

460
00:33:41,830 --> 00:33:43,360
Saving him is what matters.

461
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:46,550
If he isn't back

462
00:33:47,270 --> 00:33:48,550
within 3 days,

463
00:33:50,030 --> 00:33:51,290
then that's just fate.

464
00:33:52,830 --> 00:33:54,480
Well, I refuse to believe in fate.

465
00:33:54,480 --> 00:33:55,940
I'll find a way to save him.

466
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:56,560
Director.

467
00:33:57,550 --> 00:33:58,790
When I went in,

468
00:33:58,920 --> 00:34:00,550
Chief Yu was already dead.

469
00:34:02,480 --> 00:34:03,440
Who killed him?

470
00:34:03,440 --> 00:34:04,160
No idea.

471
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,220
Still investigating.

472
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:10,540
If even you don't know,

473
00:34:11,550 --> 00:34:12,800
then nobody does.

474
00:34:15,590 --> 00:34:17,389
As long as Yu can't talk anymore,

475
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:19,219
that's enough.

476
00:34:20,670 --> 00:34:22,110
As for Inspector Su,

477
00:34:22,710 --> 00:34:24,840
shouldn't we give her an explanation?

478
00:34:29,460 --> 00:34:31,389
Didn't you just arrest a young man?

479
00:34:31,630 --> 00:34:32,190
Yes.

480
00:34:33,110 --> 00:34:35,400
But I think besides him,

481
00:34:35,400 --> 00:34:36,320
there might be others...

482
00:34:36,320 --> 00:34:37,320
Let's go with him.

483
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:40,110
We need to wrap this up

484
00:34:40,110 --> 00:34:41,320
as soon as possible

485
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:43,340
to avoid further complications.

486
00:34:43,760 --> 00:34:44,489
Understood.

487
00:34:50,710 --> 00:34:52,000
You're framing me!

488
00:35:03,630 --> 00:35:04,320
Mr. Zhao.

489
00:35:06,150 --> 00:35:08,280
Is this the guy who killed Director Yu?

490
00:35:11,380 --> 00:35:12,790
[Confession]

491
00:35:12,920 --> 00:35:14,250
He doesn't look like it.

492
00:35:14,790 --> 00:35:15,620
Who cares?

493
00:35:19,070 --> 00:35:20,670
Now that Director Yu's out of the picture,

494
00:35:20,670 --> 00:35:24,070
you, Director Zhao, will be
sitting in that chair from now on.

495
00:35:24,070 --> 00:35:25,070
How great is that.

496
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:27,730
That's not an easy seat to fill.

497
00:35:27,880 --> 00:35:28,680
Don't jinx me.

498
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:32,240
What's Director Li
planning to do with him?

499
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:36,380
Will Inspector Su go along with this?

500
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:38,060
Dead men tell no tales.

501
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:40,130
She'll have to go along with it.

502
00:35:48,550 --> 00:35:50,550
It wasn't Cang Guanglian who did it?

503
00:35:51,180 --> 00:35:52,510
I don't think it was him.

504
00:35:54,150 --> 00:35:56,110
Yu Yingxiang was strangled to death.

505
00:35:56,110 --> 00:35:57,230
I followed Cang Guanglian in—

506
00:35:57,230 --> 00:35:59,030
we were less than a minute apart.

507
00:35:59,150 --> 00:36:01,480
A person being strangled would struggle.

508
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:06,150
So Yu Yingxiang was already dead

509
00:36:06,150 --> 00:36:07,950
before Cang Guanglian arrived.

510
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:15,230
It seems Li Moqun had long since decided

511
00:36:15,230 --> 00:36:16,550
to silence him.

512
00:36:21,360 --> 00:36:23,760
Yu Yingxiang was Li Moqun's chief steward.

513
00:36:24,510 --> 00:36:26,970
He not only masterminded the assassination

514
00:36:27,030 --> 00:36:29,430
but likely committed other crimes as well.

515
00:36:30,060 --> 00:36:33,260
He knew all along that
you were following Cang Guanglian.

516
00:36:34,360 --> 00:36:36,150
Talk about feigning one thing

517
00:36:36,150 --> 00:36:37,350
while doing another.

518
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:40,840
Cang Guanglian arrested a suspect,

519
00:36:40,840 --> 00:36:42,240
An acquaintance of ours.

520
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:43,670
Who?

521
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:45,730
Chen Kailai.

522
00:36:49,400 --> 00:36:51,200
What does he have to do with this?

523
00:36:51,650 --> 00:36:53,580
The bathhouse owner is his friend,

524
00:36:53,760 --> 00:36:55,960
and he was at the scene when it happened.

525
00:36:58,110 --> 00:36:59,970
That guy really has some bad luck.

526
00:37:00,710 --> 00:37:02,710
The murder was arranged by Li Moqun,

527
00:37:04,150 --> 00:37:05,150
but the poor guy

528
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:07,300
ended up as the scapegoat.

529
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:10,280
There was another face at the scene.

530
00:37:14,030 --> 00:37:14,760
Who?

531
00:37:37,480 --> 00:37:38,280
Inspector Su.

532
00:37:39,280 --> 00:37:40,320
Visiting so late—

533
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:42,850
is there something urgent?

534
00:37:50,190 --> 00:37:51,450
You don't remember me?

535
00:37:54,870 --> 00:37:55,540
I do.

536
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:04,800
Can you help me this once?

537
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:06,630
How?

538
00:38:08,870 --> 00:38:10,730
Your boss, Yu Yingxiang, is dead.

539
00:38:12,510 --> 00:38:13,190
I'm aware.

540
00:38:13,630 --> 00:38:16,440
Did he usually like to go to Fairy Bath?

541
00:38:19,190 --> 00:38:21,650
How would I know
my superior's whereabouts?

542
00:38:22,030 --> 00:38:23,230
When he died,

543
00:38:24,710 --> 00:38:26,240
you were there at the scene.

544
00:38:32,230 --> 00:38:35,160
Inspector Su, you don't suspect
I killed him, do you?

545
00:38:43,150 --> 00:38:44,210
I went to take a bath

546
00:38:45,550 --> 00:38:47,950
and somehow turned myself
into a murderer?

547
00:38:49,110 --> 00:38:50,570
Murder requires a motive,

548
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,200
Inspector Su.

549
00:38:57,760 --> 00:38:58,670
Do you have one?

550
00:39:03,800 --> 00:39:04,360
No.

551
00:39:06,070 --> 00:39:07,190
Li Moqun does.

552
00:39:07,710 --> 00:39:08,960
If Director Li were going to do it,

553
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:10,020
he wouldn't use me.

554
00:39:11,070 --> 00:39:12,110
He has his own people.

555
00:39:12,110 --> 00:39:13,230
Who would he use?

556
00:39:14,230 --> 00:39:14,920
No idea.

557
00:39:21,110 --> 00:39:23,110
That photographer, Chen Kailai—

558
00:39:24,340 --> 00:39:25,540
does he have a motive?

559
00:39:28,800 --> 00:39:30,800
Chen Kailai has already confessed.

560
00:39:31,850 --> 00:39:32,770
Confessed?

561
00:39:35,760 --> 00:39:37,020
Is there any evidence?

562
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:39,440
I don't know.

563
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:41,490
You'd have to ask Captain Cang.

564
00:39:42,710 --> 00:39:45,510
And the execution should be carried out
very soon.

565
00:39:52,230 --> 00:39:53,160
You've changed,

566
00:39:54,440 --> 00:39:55,280
Mr. Zhao.

567
00:40:00,710 --> 00:40:01,480
So have you,

568
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:04,120
Inspector Su.

569
00:40:11,840 --> 00:40:12,840
He's a decent guy.

570
00:40:15,920 --> 00:40:17,720
It'd be a shame if he really died.

571
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:35,670
I'm leaving

572
00:40:37,110 --> 00:40:37,920
for France.

573
00:40:41,110 --> 00:40:42,570
How about giving me a gift?

574
00:40:44,350 --> 00:40:44,900
This.

575
00:41:12,840 --> 00:41:15,040
I'll return it to you when we meet again.

576
00:41:49,230 --> 00:41:50,630
You killed Yu Yingxiang.

577
00:41:54,920 --> 00:41:56,250
Who ordered you to do it?

578
00:41:58,150 --> 00:41:58,880
It wasn't me.

579
00:42:03,510 --> 00:42:05,240
Why were you at the crime scene?

580
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:09,530
Who are you, anyway?

581
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:11,960
I'm a photographer.

582
00:42:13,320 --> 00:42:14,400
I only take photos.

583
00:42:15,190 --> 00:42:16,320
I don't kill people.

584
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:28,380
But you confessed.

585
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:32,840
I didn't.

586
00:42:33,790 --> 00:42:36,720
You forced me to put my fingerprints
on the document.

587
00:42:50,280 --> 00:42:51,480
I didn't kill anyone.

588
00:42:54,070 --> 00:42:55,670
I didn't kill anyone!

589
00:42:57,630 --> 00:42:59,440
I didn't kill anyone!
